This template generates a table of money making guides related to the subject page. It is a successor to the messagebox [[RuneScape:Requests for deletion/Template:HasMMG|Template:HasMMG deleted after a Request for Deletion]].

==Usage==
Giving a money making guide subpage name:

<code><nowiki>{{Mmgsection|Killing the King Black Dragon}}</nowiki></code>
{{Mmgsection|Killing the King Black Dragon}}

----
Giving a recurring money making guide subpage name:

<code><nowiki>{{Mmgsection|Farming ranarr weed}}</nowiki></code>
{{Mmgsection|Farming ranarr weed}}

----
Override using the page name in prose:

<code><nowiki>{{Mmgsection|Killing the King Black Dragon|mobname=the King Black Dragon}}</nowiki></code>
{{Mmgsection|Killing the King Black Dragon|mobname=the King Black Dragon}}

----
Listing multiple money making guides:

<code><nowiki>{{Mmgsection|Killing Vorkath (Toxic blowpipe)|Killing Vorkath (Dragon hunter crossbow)|Killing Vorkath (Dragon hunter lance)}}</nowiki></code>
{{Mmgsection|Killing Vorkath (Toxic blowpipe)|Killing Vorkath (Dragon hunter crossbow)|Killing Vorkath (Dragon hunter lance)}}

----
Listing multiple money making guides, ordering by a skill requirement:

<code><nowiki>{{Mmgsection|mobname=Salvaging|sort=sailing|Salvaging Small Shipwrecks|Salvaging Fisherman's Shipwrecks|Salvaging Barracuda Shipwrecks|Salvaging Large Shipwrecks|Salvaging Pirate Shipwrecks|Salvaging Mercenary Shipwrecks|Salvaging Fremennik Shipwrecks|Salvaging Merchant Shipwrecks}}</nowiki></code>
{{Mmgsection|mobname=Salvaging|sort=sailing|Salvaging Small Shipwrecks|Salvaging Fisherman's Shipwrecks|Salvaging Barracuda Shipwrecks|Salvaging Large Shipwrecks|Salvaging Pirate Shipwrecks|Salvaging Mercenary Shipwrecks|Salvaging Fremennik Shipwrecks|Salvaging Merchant Shipwrecks}}



----
Listing both normal and recurring money making guides:

<code><nowiki>{{Mmgsection|Killing demonic gorillas|Farming ranarr weed}}</nowiki></code>
{{Mmgsection|Killing demonic gorillas|Farming ranarr weed}}

{{TemplateData|<templatedata>
{
	"params": {
		"mobname": {
			"type": "string",
			"description": "Name to append onto the preface text above the guides"
		},
		"sort": {
			"type": "string",
			"description": "What to sort by. Accepted values are: 'profit', or any skill name (e.g 'sailing')"
		},
		"order": {
			"type": "string",
			"description": "Sort order when sorting. Accepted values are: 'asc', 'desc'"
		}
	},
	"description": "This template generates a table of money making guides related to the subject page.",
	"format": "inline"
}
</templatedata>}}

{{Documentation}}

This template works the same as the old template:2x and 3x but makes it possible to insert any number of times it should be repeated. To use it, insert {{t|Multi|text to be repeated|amount of times}} for example: {{t|Multi|Hi!|5}} results in:

{{Multi|Hi!|5}}

'''NOTE:''' To insert a space at the beginning or the end of a repeating, use <code>&amp;nbsp;</code>

This template currently works until 1399 repeatings.

{{Documentation}}

The '''MusicList''' template is used to easily create a list of music tracks that are unlocked in a specific location.

==Usage==
<pre>
{{MusicList
|Trahaearn Toil|Unlocked upon entering the Trahaearn mine.
|Sea Shanty 2|This track unlocks in Port Sarim.
|The Gauntlet (music track)|This track unlocks upon entering [[The Gauntlet]].
}}
</pre>

results in:
{{MusicList
|Trahaearn Toil|Unlocked upon entering the Trahaearn mine.
|Sea Shanty 2|This track unlocks in Port Sarim.
|The Gauntlet (music track)|This track unlocks upon entering [[The Gauntlet]].
}}

{{Documentation}}

This template takes a list of unnamed parameters that specify polygons on the world map, prefixed by the [[music]] track name. For relevant music tracks, the popup text when clicking on the track's polygon will omit the <code>(music track)</code> page suffix. Example:

<pre>
{{Music map|width=300|height=300|x=3232|y=3232|align=right|zoom=0
|categories=Category:Free-to-play music
}}
</pre>

{{Music map|width=300|height=300|x=3232|y=3232|align=right|zoom=0
|categories=Category:Free-to-play music
}}

This template may also take a <code>nopreprocess</code> parameter if the output should not be processed into a map.

The template also has an optional <code>bucket</code> parameter which can be set to <code>hist</code> to obtain the historical map data where available, or <code>onlyhist</code> to only obtain the historical data, and ignore all current maps.

{{TemplateData|<templatedata>
{
	"params": {
		"categories": {
			"label": "Categories",
