==Usage==
This template exactly like [[Template:CiteNPC]], with two exceptions. First, it is '''not''' a reference template in the sense that it does not create footnote-styled references. Instead, it creates the same text that {{t|CiteNPC}} would as a non-reference. This is desirable if a certain NPC-quote is the source of the majority of an article, as having the same reference at the end of every sentence. Second, it does not have the "name" parameter, as this only applies to footnote-style references.

<pre>{{PlainCiteNPC|npc=|loc=|quote=|notes=}}</pre>

===npc===
The name of the [[Non-player character]] being cited.
{{Clear|left}}

===loc===
The name of the [[Quest]], [[Holiday event]], or other piece of game content ''during'' or ''after'' which the NPC says the quote being cited, if applicable. Note that this is not the location that the NPC can be found. Set to "no" if the NPC does not say the quote during any specific event.

===quote===
What the NPC says that is being cited, quoted verbatim. Try to keep this short but relevant.

{{References standard parameters|plain}}
{{citations}}
<includeonly>[[Category:Reference templates]]</includeonly>

{{Documentation}}
__TOC__
==Usage==
<pre>{{PlainCiteNews|author=|url=|title=|newsdate=|notes=}}</pre>

This template exactly like [[Template:CiteNews]], with two exceptions. First, it is '''not''' a reference template in the sense that it does not create footnote-styled references. Instead, it creates the same text that {{t|CiteNews}} would as a non-reference. This is desirable if a certain news update is the source of the majority of an article, as having the same reference at the end of every sentence. Second, it does not have the "name" parameter, as this only applies to footnote-style references.

===url===
The full URL to the news post, including the <nowiki>https://</nowiki>. An archive of past news posts can be found [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/archive?oldschool=1 here].

===title===
The title of the news post, found between the two arrow buttons at the top.

===newsdate===
The date the news update was posted. Found next to the title between the two arrow buttons.

===quote===
A quote of what was said inside the news post.

===author===
The author of the news update. This usually appears at the bottom of the news post, before the "In Other News..." section.

{{References standard parameters|plain}}
<!-- Keep in sync with Main cite -->
{{TemplateData|<templatedata>
{
	"params": {
		"author": {
			"description": "The author of the newspost. This parameter should only be filled if the newspost has not been authored by the Old School team.",
			"example": " ",
			"type": "string"
		},
		"url": {
			"description": "The URL of the newspost",
			"example": "https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/new-client-update-clue-scroll-helper?oldschool=1",
			"type": "url",
			"label": "URL",
			"required": true
		},
		"quote": {
			"description": "Text being quoted from the newspost.",
			"type": "string"
		},
		"title": {
			"description": "Newspost's title",
			"example": "New Client Update: Clue Scroll Helper",
			"type": "line",
			"required": true
		},
		"newsdate": {
			"description": "The date the newspost was published (DD Month YYYY)",
			"example": "8 April 2020",
			"type": "date",
			"required": true
		}
	},
	"description": "Used to create a reference to a Old School RuneScape website newspost.",
	"paramOrder": [
		"author",
		"url",
		"title",
		"newsdate",
		"quote"
	],
	"format": "inline"
}
</templatedata>}}
{{citations}}
<includeonly>[[Category:Reference templates]]</includeonly>

{{Documentation}}
__NOTOC__
==Usage==
Remember to only cite tweets made by Jagex-approved accounts. A list may be found [https://xcancel.com/i/lists/188536920/members here].
<pre>{{PlainCiteTwitter|author=|url=|quote=|date=|notes=|name=}}</pre>

===author===
The author of the tweet(s). Include "Mod" prefixes, such as "Mod Mark" instead of simply "Mark". Use their mod name rather than their twitter name.

===url===
The url of the tweet in question. In case of multiple tweets, use the url of the first one in the conversation that is being cited.

===quote===
The exact transcript of the tweet(s) in question. In case of multiple tweets, cite them as one. Exclude tags (#example) and replies (@example)

===date===
The date the tweet was posted in the format dd month yyyy.

